---

<Base title="OpenTUI - A Reference Manual for Native Terminal Interfaces">
  <div class="editorial-wrapper">
    <div class="editorial-container">

      <!-- Quiet Editorial Masthead -->
      <div class="editorial-masthead">
        <div class="editorial-masthead-title">REFERENCE MANUAL // ZIG 0.14 CORE &middot; C ABI</div>
        <div class="editorial-masthead-nav">
          <a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a>
          <a href="#lab">Laboratory</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Documentation</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero Header: Logo in H1 Spot -->
      <header class="editorial-hero">
        <h1 class="hero-brand-heading">
          <OpenTUILogo class="hero-logo-large" />
          <span class="sr-only">OpenTUI</span>
        </h1>
        <h2 class="editorial-subtitle">
          A reference manual for native terminal user interfaces.
        </h2>
        <p class="editorial-lead-desc">
          An in-depth specification for building high-framerate, flicker-free terminal applications on a native Zig core with TypeScript bindings, Yoga flexbox, and 24-bit TrueColor SIMD matrices.
        </p>
        <div class="editorial-byline">
          <div>Written and engineered by the <span>OpenTUI Contributors</span>.</div>
          <div>Version 0.5.1 &middot; 58 Chapters</div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Editorial Multi-Column Flow with Masterpiece Vector Figures -->
      <div class="editorial-flow">
        
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          Have you ever wondered how a terminal screen knows how to render rich, interactive user interfaces at sixty frames per second without flickering? In classical computing, the terminal is not a bitmap canvas with hardware scanouts; it is a stream of character cells transmitted over standard input and output pipes. When a modern application updates its state, re-emitting the entire terminal grid saturates the pseudo-terminal buffer, causing severe screen tearing and latency.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_01: The Anatomy of a Character Cell -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_01</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ 24-BYTE CELL STRIDE ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 420 240" width="420" height="240" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Isometric Box Layer 1: UTF-32 Codepoint (4B) -->
              <g transform="translate(50, 16)">
                <path d="M120 10 L220 62 L120 114 L20 62 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M20 62 L20 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.14)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M220 62 L220 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.20)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                
                <line x1="120" y1="40" x2="260" y2="40" stroke="var(--cobalt-600)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
                <circle cx="120" cy="40" r="2" fill="var(--cobalt-600)"/>
                <text x="265" y="43" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--cobalt-600)">0x00: char (u32, 4B)</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Isometric Layer 2: 24-Bit FG & BG RGBA ([4]u16 = 8B each) -->
              <g transform="translate(50, 46)">
                <path d="M120 10 L220 62 L120 114 L20 62 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M20 62 L20 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.14)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M220 62 L220 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.20)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                
                <line x1="120" y1="62" x2="260" y2="88" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
                <circle cx="120" cy="62" r="2" fill="var(--emerald-600)"/>
                <text x="265" y="91" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--emerald-600)">0x04: fg &amp; bg (16B)</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Isometric Layer 3: Style Attributes (4B) -->
              <g transform="translate(50, 76)">
                <path d="M120 10 L220 62 L120 114 L20 62 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M20 62 L20 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.14)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M220 62 L220 78 L120 130 L120 114 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.20)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                
                <line x1="120" y1="62" x2="260" y2="136" stroke="var(--amber-600)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
                <circle cx="120" cy="62" r="2" fill="var(--amber-600)"/>
                <text x="265" y="139" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--amber-600)">0x14: attributes (4B)</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Actual memory layout of the OpenTUI <code>Cell</code> struct in <code>buffer.zig</code>. Packed into a 24-byte contiguous stride with 4-byte UTF-32 codepoints, dual 8-byte <code>[4]u16</code> RGBA color vectors, and 4-byte attribute bitmasks.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">OPENTUI CORE</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">STRIDE: 24B</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Because the terminal is arranged as a discrete matrix of rows and columns, a character is not merely a scalar glyph. It is a 24-byte struct containing a UTF-32 code point, a 24-bit TrueColor foreground vector (packed as <code>[4]u16</code> in linear color space), a 24-bit background vector, and a 32-bit typography bitfield for bold, italic, underline, inverse, and hyperlinks. On an 80&times;24 terminal, a single buffer of 1,920 cells occupies exactly <strong>46,080 bytes</strong> (45 KB), and the double-buffered matrix occupies ~90 KB.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_02: The Differential Damage Loop -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_02</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ DIFFERENTIAL DAMAGE LOOP ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 180" width="380" height="180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Buffer A -->
              <rect x="20" y="30" width="110" height="85" fill="var(--background)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="75" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">PREVIOUS BUFFER (45 KB)</text>
              <line x1="20" y1="58" x2="130" y2="58" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
              <line x1="20" y1="86" x2="130" y2="86" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

              <!-- Diff Arrow -->
              <path d="M145 72 L185 72" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
              <text x="165" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--emerald-600)">CELL DIFF</text>

              <!-- Buffer B with Damage Box -->
              <rect x="200" y="30" width="110" height="85" fill="var(--background)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="255" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">CURRENT BUFFER (45 KB)</text>
              <rect x="220" y="45" width="50" height="30" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15)" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="245" y="63" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--emerald-600)">DIRTY REGION</text>

              <!-- Escape Stream Output -->
              <rect x="20" y="135" width="290" height="28" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.03)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8"/>
              <text x="30" y="153" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">{"\\x1b[4;12H\\x1b[38;2;16;185;129mACTIVE\\x1b[0m"}</text>
              <text x="300" y="153" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--emerald-600)">DELTA ESCAPES</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Double-buffered cell diffing compares previous and current frames. OpenTUI isolates modified runs and emits concise ANSI cursor hops, transmitting only modified characters instead of repainting the entire grid.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">DAMAGE TRACKING</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">VT100 DELTA</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          To achieve 60 FPS motion without screen tearing, OpenTUI compares double-buffered cells on every tick. The engine checks row equality and cell attributes, tracks active SGR color state to avoid repeating identical escape codes across horizontal runs, and emits ANSI cursor positioning jumps (<code>{"\\x1b[y;xH"}</code>) only for modified cells. When a status indicator changes state, only the modified bytes are transmitted, avoiding full-screen repaints.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_03: Continuous Flexbox to Discrete Grid Quantization -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_03</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ YOGA GRID QUANTIZATION ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 170" width="380" height="170" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Continuous Float Box -->
              <rect x="30" y="30" width="140" height="70" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08)" stroke="var(--cobalt-600)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
              <text x="100" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--cobalt-600)">FLOAT: w=33.333% (15.998)</text>

              <!-- Quantization Arrow -->
              <path d="M185 65 L215 65" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
              <text x="200" y="55" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="currentColor">FLOOR(X)</text>

              <!-- Discrete Integer Cells -->
              <g transform="translate(225, 30)">
                <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="70" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.15)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <line x1="26" y1="0" x2="26" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="52" y1="0" x2="52" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="78" y1="0" x2="78" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="104" y1="0" x2="104" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <text x="65" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">16 COLUMNS</text>
              </g>
              
              <!-- Rulers -->
              <text x="190" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--text-muted)">UNICODE 16.0 WCWIDTH: 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 (2 CH) &middot; CJK (2 CH)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Compiling continuous Yoga CSS flexbox geometry into integer terminal cells without edge collisions or text clipping.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">YOGA LAYOUT</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">CSS &rarr; GRID</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Or perhaps you have wondered how web-style CSS layout can exist inside a terminal without a browser engine? Web flexbox operates in continuous subpixel coordinates (33.333% width, 1.5rem padding). But a terminal screen is an immutable integer matrix. OpenTUI embeds the native <strong>Yoga C engine</strong> and executes an exact quantization pass: fractional bounds snap to integer boundaries, border strokes share single-cell seams, and text wrapping dynamically evaluates Unicode 16.0 grapheme widths (<code>wcwidth</code>) including zero-width joiners.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_04: 4x4 RGBA SIMD Vector Lane Transformation -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_04</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ 4×4 SIMD VECTOR LANES ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 160" width="380" height="160" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Matrix Equation -->
              <g transform="translate(30, 25)">
                <!-- Left Vector -->
                <text x="15" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">R'</text>
                <text x="15" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">G'</text>
                <text x="15" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">B'</text>
                <text x="15" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">A'</text>
                <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M25 10 L30 10 L30 95 L25 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                
                <text x="45" y="55" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">=</text>

                <!-- 4x4 Matrix -->
                <g transform="translate(65, 0)">
                  <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <path d="M145 10 L150 10 L150 95 L145 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <text x="20" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.39</text>
                  <text x="55" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.76</text>
                  <text x="90" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.18</text>
                  <text x="125" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  
                  <text x="20" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.34</text>
                  <text x="55" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.68</text>
                  <text x="90" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.16</text>
                  <text x="125" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>

                  <text x="20" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.27</text>
                  <text x="55" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.53</text>
                  <text x="90" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.13</text>
                  <text x="125" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>

                  <text x="20" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="55" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="90" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="125" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">1.00</text>
                </g>

                <!-- Input Vector -->
                <g transform="translate(230, 0)">
                  <text x="15" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">R</text>
                  <text x="15" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">G</text>
                  <text x="15" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">B</text>
                  <text x="15" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">A</text>
                  <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <path d="M25 10 L30 10 L30 95 L25 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                </g>
              </g>
              <text x="190" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--amber-600)">SIMD 4-WIDE LINEAR ALGEBRA (SEPIA_MATRIX)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Linear algebra vector transformations executed across 4-wide SIMD lanes. Real-time color grading, sepia transformation, and tint masks without re-evaluating the component tree.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">COLOR PIPELINE</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">SIMD 4×4</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Before character cells are serialized into ANSI truecolor sequences, OpenTUI applies vectorized linear algebra across foreground and background color vectors using SIMD lanes: [R', G', B', A']ᵀ = M₄ₓ₄ &middot; [R, G, B, A]ᵀ. As exposed in <code>color-matrix.mdx</code> via <code>colorMatrixUniform</code>, this processes 4 channels simultaneously in native CPU vector registers.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_05: Terminal Graphics Protocol Resolution -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_05</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ GRAPHICS PROTOCOL RESOLUTION ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 150" width="380" height="150" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Tier 1 -->
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.1)" stroke="var(--cobalt-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="57" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 1</text>
              <text x="57" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--cobalt-600)">KITTY</text>
              <text x="57" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">APC PNG/RGB</text>

              <!-- Tier 2 -->
              <rect x="105" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.1)" stroke="var(--amber-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="142" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 2</text>
              <text x="142" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--amber-600)">SIXEL</text>
              <text x="142" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">6-PX BANDS</text>

              <!-- Tier 3 -->
              <rect x="190" y="20" width="85" height="85" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1)" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="232" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 3</text>
              <text x="232" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--emerald-600)">QUADRANT</text>
              <text x="232" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">▀ ▄ █ HALF-BLOCK</text>

              <!-- Tier 4 -->
              <rect x="285" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.03)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="322" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 4</text>
              <text x="322" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="currentColor">ASCII</text>
              <text x="322" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">░ ▒ ▓ HALFTONE</text>
              
              <text x="190" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--text-muted)">RUNTIME DEC / OSC CAPABILITY PROBING</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Automatic protocol negotiation. OpenTUI queries the host emulator at startup and dynamically routes between Kitty graphics protocols, DEC Sixel scanlines, and Unicode quadrant half-blocks.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">PROTOCOL RESOLUTION</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">AUTODETECT</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Terminal graphic capabilities vary widely across platforms. OpenTUI probes terminal device attributes at startup and dynamically routes between Kitty graphics (PNG/RGB chunking over APC escapes), Sixel 6-pixel raster bands, and Unicode 2&times;2 quadrant half-block characters (<code>▀▄█</code>) with 24-bit TrueColor foreground and background.
        </p>

        <p>
          All of this machinery is unified through a <strong>zero-allocation C ABI</strong> written in native Zig. Whether you construct terminal applications with declarative React 19 JSX, Solid.js fine-grained signals, or bare-metal Zig, the rendering engine operates with zero garbage collection pauses and deterministic memory lifetimes.
        </p>

      </div>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           TABLE OF CONTENTS: V1.0 ARCHIVAL INDEX
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="toc-section" id="toc">
        <div class="toc-header">
          <h2 class="toc-heading">Table of Contents.</h2>
          <span class="toc-version">SPECIFICATION INDEX</span>
        </div>

        <div class="toc-grid">
          {tocData.map((part) => (
            <div class="toc-part-card">
              <div class="toc-part-label">{part.part}</div>
              <ul class="toc-chapter-list">
                {part.chapters.map((chap) => (
                  <li class="toc-chapter-item">
                    <a href={chap.slug}>
                      <span>{chap.title}</span>
                      <span class="chapter-words">{chap.words}</span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           INTERACTIVE LABORATORY DRAFTING BENCH (REAL IN-BROWSER MATH & DIFF ENGINE)
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="bench-section" id="lab">
        <div class="bench-header">
          <h2 class="bench-heading">Interactive Laboratory.</h2>
